The function f is defined by f(x) = a(3.1)^{x+b} where a and b are integer constants and 0 < a < b. The functions g and h are equivalent to function f, where k and m are constants. Which of the following equations displays the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane as a constant or coefficient?
I. g(x) = a(3.1)^{x+k}
II. h(x) = m(3.1)^x
